Add the `allows` option to `node-dependencies/compat-engines`: a list of package names to skip.
Neither the listed packages nor their dependencies are checked, also when they're found deeper in the
tree with `deep`. An alias like `"ts7": "npm:typescript@^7"` is skipped when either its name or the
package it points to is listed.

Same change as in the upstream PR (only the rule code, without docs and tests):
https://github.com/ota-meshi/eslint-plugin-node-dependencies/pull/312

